**Explanation of the key changes**

| Change | Reason |
|--------|--------|
| **State lifted to `App`** | Guarantees the draft and notes stay alive when the user flips routes – the state lives in a parent that never unmounts. |
| **Initial load from `localStorage`** (`useState` initializer) | Restores notes & draft on page refresh. |
| **`useEffect` to write back** | Keeps data in sync across tabs/windows and after reloads. |
| **Guard `if (!draft.trim())`** | Prevents creating empty notes – also stops accidental double‑saves if the user presses `<Enter>` twice. |
| **`Date.now().toString()` ID** | Simple, deterministic, and unique for each save. (If you prefer `crypto.randomUUID()`, replace.) |
| **Single‑append `setNotes(prev => [...prev, newNote])`** | Guarantees exactly one note per save, never overwrites previous notes. |
| **Clear draft (`setDraft('')`) + remove from storage** | Draft disappears after a successful save and won’t reappear on refresh. |
| **`useCallback` on `saveNote`** | Stabilises the function reference so child components don’t cause unnecessary re‑renders. |

