**Fix Pocket Notes – Action Plan & Patch**

Below is a complete, tool‑agnostic workflow that will make the unfinished draft survive view switches and page reloads, guarantee exactly‑one‑note‑per‑save, keep existing notes intact, preserve distinctness, and leave the UI unchanged.

---

## 1️⃣ INVESTIGATION – What to examine (no tools → manual audit)

| # | What to look for | Why it matters |
|---|------------------|||
| 1 | **State definitions** – find where `draft` and `notes` are declared (`useState`, `this.state`, Vue `data`, etc.). | If they live only in a component that unmounts on route change, they disappear. |
| 2 | **Persistence code** – any `localStorage.getItem/setItem`, `sessionStorage`, or `IndexedDB` usage. | Without persistence the draft & notes vanish on refresh. |
| 3 | **Routing logic** – `<Route>` components, `<Link>` usage, any custom navigation helpers. | Determines whether the “Draft” component ever unmounts. |
| 4 | **Save handler** – the function that creates a new note (`onClick`, `onKeyDown`, debounce, etc.). | Duplicate notes usually stem from multiple triggers or missing guards. |
| 5 | **ID generation** – how note IDs are produced (`Date.now()`, random string, etc.). | Must be deterministic & unique to avoid accidental overwrites. |
| 6 | **UI structure** – CSS class names, HTML tags, any inline styles that give the app its look. | We must not change visual design. |
| 7 | **Any other state** – e.g., a “loading” flag, error handling, that could reset the draft. | Edge‑cases that might wipe the draft. |

**Quick manual steps (open DevTools → Sources → search):**
- `Ctrl+F` for `draft` and `notes`.
- Look for `useEffect`, `addEventListener('beforeunload')`, `localStorage`.
